# wip — vscode-lsp-integration
# Branch: feature/vscode-lsp-integration
# Started: 2026-02-20

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Integrate the native node-based Spw language server into the VS Code extension, replacing flaky regex heuristics with rigorous AST/semantic knowledge for site-codebase adoption."
 ~#taste: "correctness and expressiveness by centralizing language intelligence in the semantic core, preventing divergence between the editor and compiler."
}

^["stream"]{
 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 # Types: observe, decide, surprise, revise, blocked, taste, rebase, hygiene
 >>[2026-02-20 05:15] observe — SpwLspHandler existing implementation supports hover, outline, and definition, but VSCode extension currently uses regex.
 >>[2026-02-20 05:15] decide — Transition the extension to use vscode-languageclient, connecting via stdio to scripts/lsp/stdio-server.ts.
 >>[2026-02-22 10:10] revise — Added agentic hygiene preflight: mandatory rebase against origin/main and hygiene split for unrelated drift before commit 1.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:45] observe — codebase restructured since plan was filed: LSP now lives in packages/spw-lsp/src/ (handlers/, stdio-server.ts, context.ts, types.ts); seed/parser in packages/spw-seed/src/; extension already has vscode-languageclient ^9.0.1 installed and LanguageClient initialized. Prior commits ~[1]-~[6] are substantially complete.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:46] revise — rebase target updated from lore-era f53934f to current main@3b1747c4. File paths updated throughout. Commits ~[1]-~[6] marked as landed; remaining work starts at ~[7].
 >>[2026-03-27 00:47] decide — for site codebase installation: the LSP must work standalone via `npm run lsp` (already resolved by lsp-lore-upstream-bridge) and the extension must be publishable to VS Code Marketplace. Commit ~[27] (release declaration) should include marketplace metadata.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:48] taste — site codebases will experience spw through the extension first. The quality of hover, completions, and document links directly shapes first impressions. Prioritize correctness over breadth: completions and rename are more valuable than experimental operator injection for initial external adoption.
 >>[2026-03-27 12:55] observe — Commit 7 (maintain regex DocumentLinkProvider) skipped as extension already moved fully to LSP links. Commit 8 (LSP architecture docs) and Commit 9 (path literal highlighting) completed.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:28] revise — narrow this plan to the editor-reliability lane for site installation. Experimental operator injection is deferred to a separate syntax branch once install/docs/dx surfaces stop moving.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:29] decide — parallelize the remaining work into two tracks after commit 10: language-service correctness (completions, rename, hover) and editor cleanup/docs (document links, extension cleanup, capability docs, release truth).
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. Remove when resolved (log resolution in stream first).
 # ?[label]: "question"
}

^["commits"]{
 # Planned commits in order. Use project sigil conventions.
 # ~[N]: "sigil[scope] — description"
 ~[1]: "&[hygiene] — rebase feature branch onto origin/main and isolate unrelated drift in a hygiene split branch"
 ~[2]: "&[lsp] — harden stdio-server with robust message partitioning and error boundaries"
 ~[3]: "![lsp] — add unit tests for stdio-server message parsing edge cases"
 ~[4]: "vocab[lsp] — strict types for LSP request/response envelopes"
 ~[5]: ".[extension] — add vscode-languageclient dependency and update npm scripts"
 ~[6]: "&[extension] — replace regex-based outline/hover with native LSP client initialization"
 ~[7]: "&[extension] — maintain regex DocumentLinkProvider while delegating other features to LSP"
 ~[8]: ".[docs] — document LSP client architecture and fallback behaviors"
 ~[9]: "&[analyzer] — parse path literals (tilde-strings, sigil-paths) into semantic tokens"
 ~[10]: "![analyzer] — verify semantic token generation for all path variants"
 ~[11]: "vocab[analyzer] — expand Symbol kind union to include file and directory types"
 ~[12]: "&[lsp] — implement context-aware completions API reading from analyzer scope"
 ~[13]: "&[lsp] — add file-system resolution to path completions within SpwLanguageService"
 ~[14]: "![lsp] — end-to-end tests for file-system auto-completions via LanguageService"
 ~[15]: "&[lsp] — implement textDocument/rename routing in SpwLspHandler"
 ~[16]: "&[analyzer] — refactor symbol resolution graph to support cascading rename edits"
 ~[17]: "&[lsp] — implement textDocument/documentLink in LSP to replace extension regex regex"
 ~[18]: "&[extension] — remove legacy regex DocumentLinkProvider now that LSP supplies links"
 ~[19]: "&[lsp] — enhance HoverProvider to perform cross-file peeking via analyzer graph"
 ~[20]: "![lsp] — verify safe cross-file reading for hover peeks"
 ~[21]: ".[docs] — update spw-feature-planning and editor ecosystem guide with new LSP capabilities"
 ~[27]: ".[release] — declare v0.2.0-alpha for VS Code extension and LSP"
}

